  "details": "Currently vrchat has the android build on steam frame only, however i got curious and set the compatibility to proton stable and was able to launch the offline test mode of pc vrchat on my steam frame standalone, and everything worked perfectly.\n\nWouldn't it be worth giving us the option to natively switch between the versions? The only thing that i think needs to be done for frame standalone is swapping the eac it comes with for the ARM64 version of EAC. If that's not hard atleast.\n\nPlenty of things work just fine, like audios, shaders, finger tracking and osc. The last two aren't on the current build. Copy and paste doesnt work but doesn't crash the game.\n\nHowever if there's more that meets the eye in terms of this compatibility then thats understandable, but it looks like pc vrchat could work standalone.",
